-- Rendered discovery diagnostics: the text a user sees for a coded row.
--
-- A diagnostic row stores a code, a span and a block of integer arguments
-- (`tables/diagnostic_code.brp` documents each code's arguments). This module
-- is the one place that turns them into a message and a help line, so the
-- wording lives in one table: one `match` over the code, which fails to
-- compile for a code without text.
--
-- It sits beside `tables/`, not in it: the text for an import that differs
-- only in letter case reuses the source provider's `respelled_import_text`,
-- and `tables/` imports no other folder. Nothing in the stage imports this
-- module; it is read by whatever shows diagnostics.
--
-- The messages of the existing compiler are copied here, not referenced: the
-- stage must not import the old compiler. `docs/DISCOVERY_TABLES_DESIGN.md`
-- lists every code whose text differs from the existing compiler's, and why.
-- Names and numbers come from the arguments and the frozen tables; the few
-- diagnostics whose subject is only a stretch of source (the name of a
-- reserved keyword, an unexpected character) read that text from the row's
-- span.
import:
	../sources/source_provider: respelled_import_text
	../tables/builder:
		DiagnosticRow,
		ImplicitDiagnosticRow,
		RootDiagnosticRow,
		SourceId,
		import_id_at_row,
		literal_id_at_row,
		name_id_at_row,
		path_id_at_row,
		root_id_at_row,
		source_id_at_row,
		source_id_index,
	../tables/diagnostic_code:
		DiscoveryDiagnosticCode(
			UnresolvedImportDiagnostic,
			SourceTooLargeDiagnostic,
			TooManySourcesDiagnostic,
			UnterminatedDocstringDiagnostic,
			UnterminatedStringDiagnostic,
